{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is cybersecurity and why is it important?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Cybersecurity involves protecting digital assets, networks, systems, and information from cyberattacks. This requires a multi-layered strategy that starts before deployment, continues through ongoing monitoring and threat detection, and extends to post-incident investigation and response. The importance of cybersecurity cannot be overstated in the age of evolving AI-powered threats and reliance on cloud-based infrastructure. Businesses and organizations worldwide depend on technology, making strong cybersecurity essential to protect data, ensure continuity, and maintain trust."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can a beginner start learning cybersecurity?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If you're curious about how to learn cybersecurity as a complete beginner, start with structured courses that combine theory with practical skills. EC-Council's Essentials Series is designed to help beginners explore cybersecurity and covers the fundamentals of various cybersecurity specializations. Along with self-paced video lessons, each Essentials Series course provides access to hands-on labs so beginners can learn real-world skills. Learners who successfully pass the proctored exam also receive a certification. For beginners, this is a good option to become familiar with cybersecurity while building skills and using tools that can help prepare them for advanced certification courses requiring experience."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need prior IT experience to enroll in cyber security courses?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No, EC-Council offers many beginner-friendly cybersecurity courses. The Essentials Series includes eight cybersecurity courses that require no prior experience in IT or related fields; even students can enroll. These courses cover the basics of network defense, ethical hacking, digital forensics, DevSecOps, SOC, cloud security, and more. You can also pursue the CCT course without prior IT experience. This certification will immerse you into the practical, skill development phase of learning across multiple cybersecurity domains and help you start your professional cybersecurity journey."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What topics are typically covered in a cyber security course?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Each EC-Council cyber security course is aligned with a specific career track. Based on the program you choose, you will gain in-depth knowledge and hands-on experience to help prepare you for real-world roles. Our certifications cover the following cybersecurity course topics: ethical hacking, penetration testing, threat intelligence, DevSecOps, cloud security, SOC, network security, encryption, AI security, application security, blockchain, computer forensics, and more."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which are the best cybersecurity courses online?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The best cybersecurity courses online are the ones that build your theoretical knowledge as well as practical skills in real-world scenarios. Look for programs with industry-aligned curricula and hands-on labs to practice in realistic environments. Also make sure the courses have a global reach, so that your qualifications are widely accepted by employers across regions. EC-Council certifications meet these criteria. They provide structured, accredited training that is recognized by global government agencies and Fortune 500 companies. Certifications such as CEH and CND align with U.S. Department of Defense baseline requirements under DoD 8140. For blue-team skills, CSA and CTIA provide operations-focused training. In the field of AI security, EC-Council offers role-based AI security certifications, such as CAIPM and CRAGE."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What jobs can I get after completing cyber security courses?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "After completing an EC-Council certification, learners may be prepared to pursue entry-level, mid-level, or leadership-oriented roles depending on the certification path, experience level, and specialization. EC-Council also offers certifications for experienced professionals, including CCISO and Associate CCISO, for those in or aspiring to executive leadership roles. To know which cybersecurity jobs are aligned with which certification, you can use the EC-Council certification learning roadmap. It helps you choose certifications based on your experience level and preferred cybersecurity domain, while showing how your path can progress over time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is EC-Council?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "EC-Council (International Council of E-Commerce Consultants) is a leading authority in cybersecurity training and certification. Founded in 2001, our mission is to improve security by validating professionals with the skills and knowledge to handle cyberattacks and related crises. We have a presence in more than 170 countries and have successfully trained more than 400,000 cybersecurity professionals."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is EC-Council a legitimate certification authority?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. EC-Council is an ISO/IEC 17024-accredited organization. Our certification programs are globally recognized by accreditation bodies, such as the American National Standards Institute (ANSI), and by many government agencies and Fortune 500 companies. The U.S. Department of Defense has approved CEH, CEH Practical, CND, ECIH, CHFI, and CCISO as certification requirements for many critical job roles in the DoD cyber workforce."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who founded EC-Council?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "EC-Council was founded by Jay Bavisi, who currently serves as Group President. The organization operates the EC-Council University (ECCU), EC-Council Global Services (EGS), and EC-Council Learning (ECL). EC-Council also provides scholarships and runs initiatives like The Hackerverse, a CTF competition open to participants worldwide."
      }
    }
  ]
}

